+# UsdtYieldVault — pre-deployment review
+
+**Verdict: do not ship this on Monday.**
+
+`deposit()` cannot succeed against the real USDT at `0xdAC17F9…ec7`. Not "might fail
+under load" — every call reverts, on every block, forever. The vault is inert on
+mainnet from the moment it is deployed.
+
+Behind that, the second problem is worse for anyone who *does* eventually use it:
+the vault never reads its own aUSDT balance, so Aave interest never reaches
+depositors and cannot be recovered by anyone. On a real mainnet fork, a 1,000,000
+USDT position earns **42,523.25 USDT** over a year and the depositor's claim moves
+by **0**.
+
+The 39 green tests do not catch either of these, because `test/mocks/MockUSDT.sol`
+is an OpenZeppelin ERC20 (which returns `bool`, unlike USDT) and
+`test/mocks/MockAavePool.sol` never pays interest. 100% line and function coverage
+on `src/UsdtYieldVault.sol` is accurate and irrelevant: every line runs, and no line
+is checked against how the real counterparties behave.
+
+Nothing under `src/` was changed. `test/UsdtYieldVault.t.sol` and `test/mocks/`
+are untouched.
+
+---
+
