+## 1. Critical — `deposit()` reverts on every call against real USDT
+
+`src/UsdtYieldVault.sol:94`:
+
+```solidity
+usdt.approve(address(aavePool), amount);
+```
+
+`usdt` is typed `IERC20`, whose `approve` is declared `returns (bool)`. solc
+therefore emits an `abi.decode(returndata, (bool))` after the call, which requires
+at least 32 bytes of return data. The deployed TetherToken's `approve` returns
+nothing. The decode fails and the whole transaction reverts.
+
+`safeTransferFrom` on line 93 is fine — `SafeERC20` tolerates empty return data.
+Line 94 is the only place the contract calls a token method directly.
+
+### Evidence — the root cause, straight off mainnet
+
+```
+$ cast call 0xdAC17F958D2ee523a2206206994597C13D831ec7 "approve(address,uint256)" \
+    0x87870Bca3F3fD6335C3F4ce8392D69350B4fA4E2 0 \
+    --from 0x5754284f345afc66a98fbB0a0Afe71e0F007B949 \
+    --block 21000000 --rpc-url https://eth.drpc.org
+0x
+```
+
+Zero bytes of return data. Same for `transfer`.
+
