+### Evidence — Aave is not the problem
+
+The identical supply, with the approve done without decoding a return value, works
+against the real pool:
+
+```
+$ forge test --match-test 'test_Fork_AaveAcceptsTheSupplyWhenApproveIsDoneCorrectly'
+[PASS] test_Fork_AaveAcceptsTheSupplyWhenApproveIsDoneCorrectly() (gas: 347636)
+```
+
+### Why the shipped suite is green
+
+`test/mocks/MockUSDT.sol` is `contract MockUSDT is ERC20` — OpenZeppelin's ERC20,
+whose `approve` returns `bool`. The suite has never executed line 94 against a token
+that behaves like USDT.
+
+### Fix
+
+Use `SafeERC20.forceApprove`, which is already imported via
+`using SafeERC20 for IERC20`:
+
+```solidity
+usdt.forceApprove(address(aavePool), amount);
+```
+
+`forceApprove` ignores empty return data *and* handles USDT's other quirk (see
+finding 11a). Do not use `usdt.approve(...)`. Also consider a one-time
+`forceApprove(pool, type(uint256).max)` in the constructor plus a top-up, to avoid an
+approve on every deposit.
