+### Evidence — stateful fuzzing
+
+```
+$ forge test --match-path 'test/audit/VaultInvariant.t.sol'
+
+Ran 1 test for test/audit/VaultInvariant.t.sol:VaultInvariantTest
+[FAIL: vault holds aUSDT that its accounting has written off: 99999000115 != 102128978817]
+	[Sequence] (original: 4, shrunk: 2)
+		sender=0x00000000000000000000000000000000000015fb addr=[test/audit/VaultInvariant.t.sol:VaultHandler]0x5991A2dF15A8F6A256D3Ec51E99254Cd3fb576A9 calldata=deposit(uint256,uint256) args=[321, 114]
+		sender=0x0000000000000000000000000000000000000807 addr=[test/audit/VaultInvariant.t.sol:VaultHandler]0x5991A2dF15A8F6A256D3Ec51E99254Cd3fb576A9 calldata=accrueInterest(uint256) args=[2833899020717238242602832079079829933437752884946 [2.833e48]]
+ invariant_NoValueIsStrandedInTheVault() (runs: 0, calls: 0, reverts: 0)
+
+Suite result: FAILED. 0 passed; 1 failed; 0 skipped; finished in 3.21ms (2.29ms CPU time)
+```
+
+Two calls to break it. The exact counterexample varies with the fuzz seed; the
+invariant fails on every run.
+
+### Fix
+
+Make `totalAssets()` read reality and delete `totalAssetsStored`:
+
+```solidity
+function totalAssets() public view returns (uint256) {
+    return aUsdt.balanceOf(address(this));
+}
+```
+
+Then `convertToShares` / `convertToAssets` use `totalAssets()`, `deposit()` computes
+shares from the pre-deposit `totalAssets()`, and `withdraw()` stops mutating an asset
+counter entirely — burning shares is enough, because the aToken balance is the source
+of truth. This is what OpenZeppelin's `ERC4626` does and it removes findings 2, 3 and
+7 in one change.
+
+Two consequences to handle deliberately:
+
+- `totalAssets()` becoming donatable re-opens the classic ERC-4626 inflation attack
+  that the current design accidentally avoids (see Controls). Mitigate it the standard
+  way — a virtual-shares offset, or seed the vault with a permanently-locked first
+  deposit at construction.
+- If you keep the internal counter instead, you must add an explicit
+  `harvest()`/`accrue()` that folds `aUsdt.balanceOf(this) - totalAssetsStored` into
+  `totalAssetsStored`, and call it at the top of `deposit()` and `withdraw()`.
+  Reading the balance directly is simpler and has fewer failure modes.
+
+Either way, add a `sweep`/`rescue` path (or at minimum an owner-callable
+`skim`) so value that ends up outside the accounting is not permanently lost.
+
