+
+## 4. High — the owner can take a user's entire deposit
+
+`setDepositFee` has no upper bound, no timelock, and takes effect on the next block:
+
+```solidity
+function setDepositFee(uint256 newFeeBps) external onlyOwner {
+    uint256 previousFeeBps = depositFeeBps;
+    depositFeeBps = newFeeBps;
+    emit DepositFeeUpdated(previousFeeBps, newFeeBps);
+}
+```
+
+An owner holding shares who sees a deposit in the mempool can front-run it with
+`setDepositFee(9_999)`. The victim's full `amount` is still supplied to Aave and still
+credited to `totalAssetsStored`, but they are minted shares for only 0.01% of it. The
+other 99.99% accrues to existing shareholders — the owner.
+
+### Evidence
+
+```
+$ forge test --match-test 'test_F05_OwnerCannotConfiscateAnInFlightDeposit' -vv
+
+[FAIL: owner captured alice's deposit: 199980 !~= 1000000000 (max delta: 1000000, real delta: 999800020)] test_F05_OwnerCannotConfiscateAnInFlightDeposit() (gas: 2692344)
+Logs:
+  alice deposited            : 1000000000
+  alice claimable after      : 199980
+  owner claimable gain       : 999800019
+```
+
+Alice deposits 1,000 USDT and can claim **0.19998 USDT**. The owner's claim goes up by
+**999.80 USDT**.
+
+```
+$ forge test --match-test 'test_F05_DepositFeeIsBounded'
+[FAIL: next call did not revert as expected] test_F05_DepositFeeIsBounded() (gas: 2399481)
+```
+
+`setDepositFee(20_000)` — a 200% fee — is accepted without complaint.
+
+### Fix
+
+- Add a hard cap enforced in both the constructor and the setter, e.g.
+  `if (newFeeBps > MAX_FEE_BPS) revert FeeTooHigh();` with `MAX_FEE_BPS = 100` (1%).
+- Put fee changes behind a timelock, or make them effective only from the next
+  epoch/block-delay, so an in-flight deposit cannot be repriced.
+- Add a `minSharesOut` argument to `deposit()` so callers can bound their own slippage
+  regardless. This also protects against benign share-price movement.
+- Move ownership to a multisig behind a `TimelockController` before deployment.
+
